7
00:00:12,142 --> 00:00:13,874
A search of the canyon the next morning

8
00:00:14,344 --> 00:00:15,606
found no wreckage at all.

9
00:00:16,176 --> 00:00:18,414
That is not a story from the 1950s.

10
00:00:18,884 --> 00:00:20,477
It happened in 2026,

11
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:23,464
and on October 23, the Pentagon published

12
00:00:23,484 --> 00:00:25,815
the government's own reports about it.

13
00:00:26,385 --> 00:00:28,532
There are two of them: one from the

14
00:00:28,552 --> 00:00:30,947
Pentagon's UFO office, and one from the

15
00:00:30,967 --> 00:00:31,194
FBI.

16
00:00:31,664 --> 00:00:33,428
And they do not tell the same story.

17
00:00:33,998 --> 00:00:35,580
So what did those agents see?

18
00:00:36,163 --> 00:00:39,170
And why did the government put it in the

19
00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:41,441
same release as a 1957 bomber,

20
00:00:42,024 --> 00:00:44,609
a Cold War memo about falling space junk,

21
00:00:45,191 --> 00:00:47,472
and a lab test on hair from a fence where

22
00:00:47,492 --> 00:00:49,493
a witness said a Skinwalker had run?

23
00:00:50,064 --> 00:00:51,108
Let's open the file.

24
00:00:57,664 --> 00:00:58,660
Start with the setting.

25
00:00:59,279 --> 00:01:00,536
The date is blacked out.

26
00:01:00,876 --> 00:01:01,786
So is the place.

27
00:01:02,256 --> 00:01:04,407
The memo, written by the All-domain

28
00:01:04,427 --> 00:01:06,951
Anomaly Resolution Office, known as AARO,

29
00:01:06,971 --> 00:01:07,881
says only this:

30
00:01:08,351 --> 00:01:11,832
2026, 8:23 in the evening, local time.

31
00:01:12,403 --> 00:01:15,093
Two federal law enforcement agents were on

32
00:01:15,113 --> 00:01:17,481
a hilltop, at what the memo calls the

33
00:01:17,501 --> 00:01:19,094
primary observation post,

34
00:01:19,565 --> 00:01:21,693
doing what it calls routine observation

35
00:01:21,713 --> 00:01:22,134
support.

36
00:01:22,703 --> 00:01:24,051
The sun had just gone down.

37
00:01:24,521 --> 00:01:26,824
The memo describes a residual sunset

38
00:01:26,844 --> 00:01:29,404
gradient behind the western ridge lines,

39
00:01:29,874 --> 00:01:31,920
while the valleys below were falling into

40
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:32,273
shadow.

41
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:34,831
Their main optical gear and their

42
00:01:34,851 --> 00:01:37,327
tripod-mounted sensors were pointed east.

43
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:39,059
The thing came from the west.

44
00:01:39,629 --> 00:01:41,830
A third witness, at a second post, was

45
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:43,992
scanning west with long-range thermal

46
00:01:44,012 --> 00:01:44,577
equipment,

47
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:47,178
picked up an object moving over the ridge

48
00:01:47,198 --> 00:01:47,440
line,

49
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:49,375
and called it out on the radio.

50
00:01:49,945 --> 00:01:52,037
The two agents immediately moved across

51
00:01:52,057 --> 00:01:53,933
the peak to get a view to the west.

52
00:01:54,403 --> 00:01:56,723
The tripod-mounted thermal system could

53
00:01:56,743 --> 00:01:59,244
not be moved quickly, so it stayed behind.

54
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:02,333
One agent had binoculars and a handheld

55
00:02:02,353 --> 00:02:03,552
thermal monocular.

56
00:02:04,122 --> 00:02:05,699
He saw it with his own eyes first,

57
00:02:06,169 --> 00:02:08,445
a dark shape against the last light in the

58
00:02:08,465 --> 00:02:09,101
western sky.

59
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,130
By the memo's account, what happened next

60
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:13,533
lasted about half a minute.

61
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:15,959
The memo splits it into three phases.

62
00:02:16,579 --> 00:02:17,308
Phase one.

63
00:02:17,778 --> 00:02:20,037
The object was climbing straight up over

64
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:22,203
the ridge, slowly and perfectly level.

65
00:02:22,673 --> 00:02:24,378
No tilt, no sway, no wobble.

66
00:02:24,848 --> 00:02:25,977
About ten seconds.

67
00:02:26,547 --> 00:02:28,435
It was matte black and did not reflect

68
00:02:28,455 --> 00:02:28,737
light.

69
00:02:29,207 --> 00:02:31,540
The memo lists everything the agents did

70
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,011
not see:

71
00:02:32,481 --> 00:02:34,951
no rotors, no rivets, no panels, no

72
00:02:34,971 --> 00:02:37,157
windows, no canopy, no exhaust.

73
00:02:37,727 --> 00:02:39,741
Its size, as the agents estimated it:

74
00:02:40,211 --> 00:02:42,114
